#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:12
msgid "Flocculation Design"
msgstr "Diseño de floculación"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:14
msgid ""
"**Important Note:** This chapter introduces uncertainty and empirical "
"design. Some of the parameters used to design AguaClara flocculators are "
"based on what has been shown to work in the field, as opposed to having been"
" derived scientifically. To make sure that the reader is aware of these "
"concepts and parameters that don’t yet have a thorough basis in research, "
"they will be highlighted in red when they appear."
msgstr ""
"**Nota importante:** Este capítulo introduce la incertidumbre y el diseño "
"empírico. Algunos de los parámetros utilizados para diseñar floculadores "
"AguaClara se basan en lo que se ha demostrado que funciona en campo, en "
"lugar de haber sido derivados científicamente. Para asegurarse de que el "
"lector conozca estos conceptos y parámetros que aún no tienen una base "
"sólida en la investigación, se resaltarán en rojo cuando aparezcan."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:16
msgid ""
"AguaClara's approach to flocculator design is the same as it is for any "
"other unit process. First, critical design criteria, called inputs, are "
"established. These criteria represent the priorities that the rest of the "
"design will be based around. Once these parameters are established, then the"
" other parameters of the design, which are dependent on the inputs, are "
"calculated based on certain constraints."
msgstr ""
"El enfoque de AguaClara para el diseño de floculadores es el mismo que para "
"cualquier otro proceso unitario. Primero, se establecen criterios críticos "
"de diseño, llamados entradas. Estos criterios representan las prioridades en"
" torno a las cuales se basará el resto del diseño. Una vez establecidos "
"estos parámetros, los demás parámetros del diseño, que dependen de las "
"entradas, se calculan en función de ciertas restricciones."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:18
msgid ""
"Take the CDC as an example of this design process in "
":ref:`title_flow_control_design`; its inputs are :math:`h_{L_{max}}`, "
":math:`\\sum K`, :math:`\\Pi_{Error}`, and the discrete dosing tube "
"diameters  :math:`D` that are available at hardware stores or pipe "
"suppliers. Its dependent variables include the number and length of the "
"dosing tubes and the flow through the CDC system."
msgstr ""
"Tomemos el CDC como ejemplo de este proceso de diseño en "
":ref:`title_flow_control_design`; sus entradas son :math:`h_{L_{max}}`, "
":math:`\\sum K`, :math:`\\Pi_{Error}`, y los diámetros discretos de los "
"tubos de dosificación  :math:`D` que están disponibles en ferreterías o "
"proveedores de tuberías. Sus variables dependientes incluyen el número y la "
"longitud de los tubos de dosificación y el flujo a través del sistema CDC."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:20
msgid ""
"The flocculator is more complex to design than the CDC, as it has more "
"details and parameters and the equations for those details and parameters "
"are very interdependent. Therefore, there are many ways to design an "
"AguaClara flocculator, and many different sets of critical design criteria "
"to begin with. Below are design approaches for several of the different "
"potential flocculator geometries."
msgstr ""
"El floculador es más complejo de diseñar que el CDC, ya que tiene más "
"detalles y parámetros y las ecuaciones para esos detalles y parámetros son "
"muy interdependientes. Por lo tanto, existen muchas formas de diseñar un "
"floculador AguaClara y muchos conjuntos diferentes de criterios críticos de "
"diseño para empezar. A continuación se presentan enfoques de diseño para "
"varias de las diferentes geometrías de posibles floculadores."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:22
msgid ""
"In all cases we will need equations relating head loss, velocity gradient, "
"viscosity, and collision potential. Flocculators must operate effectively "
"over a range of temperatures and the critical design temperature is the "
"coldest operating temperature. The viscosity shown in subsequent equations "
"is the viscosity at the coldest operating temperature."
msgstr ""
"En todos los casos necesitaremos ecuaciones que relacionen pérdida de carga,"
" gradiente de velocidad, viscosidad y potencial de colisión. Los "
"floculadores deben funcionar eficazmente en un rango de temperaturas y la "
"temperatura crítica de diseño es la temperatura de funcionamiento más baja. "
"La viscosidad mostrada en las ecuaciones posteriores es la viscosidad a la "
"temperatura de funcionamiento más baja."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:24
msgid ""
"The following equations describe the design process assuming that a velocity"
" gradient is specified for the coldest operating temperature. Given "
":math:`\\tilde{G}`, we can very easily find :math:`\\theta`:"
msgstr ""
"Las siguientes ecuaciones describen el proceso de diseño asumiendo que se "
"especifica un gradiente de velocidad para la temperatura de funcionamiento "
"más baja. Dada :math:`\\tilde{G}`, podemos encontrar fácilmente "
":math:`\\theta`:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:26
msgid "\\theta = \\frac{\\tilde{G} \\theta}{\\tilde{G}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:31
msgid ""
"Finally, we take retention time :math:`\\theta` over plant flow rate "
":math:`Q` to get the required volume of the flocculator:"
msgstr ""
"Finalmente, tomamos el tiempo de retención :math:`\\theta` sobre el caudal "
":math:`Q` de la planta para obtener el volumen requerido del floculador:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:33
msgid "\\forall_{floc} = \\theta Q"
msgstr "\\forall_{floc} = \\theta Q"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:37
msgid ""
"Now that we have the basic parameters defined, we can start to design the "
"details of the flocculator, starting from the physical dimensions."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que tenemos los parámetros básicos definidos, podemos empezar a "
"diseñar los detalles del floculador, partiendo de las dimensiones físicas."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:40
msgid "Horizontal-Horizontal flow flocculators"
msgstr "Floculadores de flujo horizontal-horizontal"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:42
msgid ""
"Horizontal-Horizontal flocculators can be easily designed to have an optimal"
" :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}`. Our current understanding is that the optimal value to"
" achieve uniform velocity gradients and to allow the flow to fully expand is"
" when :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS} = 6`. The flow geometry can be optimized to reduce "
"construction costs by varying the relationship between :math:`S` and "
":math:`W`. The dimension :math:`W` is in the vertical direction and thus "
"increasing W will increase the water depth and reduce the plan view area of "
"the flocculator. If land area is constrained and the cost of roofing is "
"considered it is very likely that the optimal solution will require "
":math:`W>S`."
msgstr ""
"Los floculadores horizontales-horizontales pueden diseñarse fácilmente para "
"tener una :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}`óptima. Nuestra comprensión actual es que el "
"valor óptimo para lograr gradientes de velocidad uniformes y permitir que el"
" flujo se expanda completamente es cuando :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS} = 6`. La "
"geometría del flujo puede optimizarse para reducir los costes de "
"construcción variando la relación entre :math:`S` y :math:`W`. La dimensión "
":math:`W` está en dirección vertical y, por tanto, aumentar W aumentará la "
"profundidad del agua y reducirá el área de vista en planta del floculador. "
"Si el área del terreno está limitada y se considera el coste del tejado, es "
"muy probable que la solución óptima requiera :math:`W>S`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:46
msgid "Horizontal-Vertical flow flocculators"
msgstr "Floculadores de flujo horizontal-vertical"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:58
msgid "Input parameters"
msgstr "Parámetros de entrada"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:49
msgid ""
"Specify: - :math:`\\tilde{G}`, velocity gradient at the coldest operating "
"temperature - :math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta`, collision potential at the coldest"
" operating temperature - :math:`Q`, plant flow rate - :math:`H`, height of "
"water *at the end of the flocculator* - :math:`L_{max, \\, sed}`, max length"
" of a flocculator channel based on clarifier length - :math:`W_{min, \\, "
"human}` minimum width of a single channel based on the width of the average "
"human hip (someone's got to go down there...)"
msgstr ""
"Especifica: - :math:`\\tilde{G}`, gradiente de velocidad a la temperatura de"
" funcionamiento más baja - :math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta`, potencial de colisión"
" a la temperatura de funcionamiento más baja - :math:`Q`, caudal planta - "
":math:`H`, altura del agua *al final del floculador* - :math:`L_{max, \\, "
"sed}`, longitud máxima de un canal floculador según la longitud del "
"clarificador - :math:`W_{min, \\, human}` ancho mínimo de un canal basado en"
" el ancho medio de la cadera humana (alguien tiene que bajar allí...)"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:56
msgid ""
"Find: - :math:`\\theta`, hydraulic retention time - :math:`\\forall_{floc}`,"
" flocculator volume - :math:`h_{L_{floc}}`, head loss (independent of "
"operating temperature)"
msgstr ""
"Hallazgo: - :math:`\\theta`, tiempo de retención hidráulica - "
":math:`\\forall_{floc}`, volumen del floculador - :math:`h_{L_{floc}}`, "
"pérdida de carga (independiente de la temperatura de funcionamiento)"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:63
msgid "Physical dimensions"
msgstr "Dimensiones físicas"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:61
msgid ""
"Calculate: - :math:`L_{channel}`, actual channel length - "
":math:`n_{channels}`, amount of channels - :math:`W_{channel}`, actual "
"channel width"
msgstr ""
"Calcular: - :math:`L_{channel}`, longitud real del canal - "
":math:`n_{channels}`, cantidad de canales - :math:`W_{channel}`, ancho real "
"del canal"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:69
msgid "Hydraulic parameters"
msgstr "Parámetros hidráulicos"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:66
msgid ""
"Calculate: - :math:`H_e`, distance between baffle/obstacle induced flow "
"expansions - :math:`n_{obstacles}`, amount of obstacles per baffle space - "
":math:`S`, baffle spacing, distance between baffles"
msgstr ""
"Calcular: - :math:`H_e`, distancia entre expansiones de flujo inducidas por "
"el deflector/obstáculo - :math:`n_{obstacles}`, cantidad de obstáculos por "
"espacio del deflector - :math:`S`, espaciado del deflector, distancia entre "
"deflectores"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:78
msgid "physical floccuation parameter"
msgstr "Parámetro físico de flocuación"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:78
msgid ""
"Flocculator geometry definition including the effect of baffle thickness. "
"Accounting for baffle thickness would be particularly important if "
"`ferrocement <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferrocement>`_ or wood were used"
" for baffles."
msgstr ""
"Definición de geometría de floculadores incluyendo el efecto del grosor del "
"deflector. Tener en cuenta el grosor del deflector sería especialmente "
"importante si se usaran `ferrocement "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferrocement>`_ o madera para los deflectores."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:82
msgid ""
"We start by making sure that our flocculator will be able to flocculate "
"effectively by defining :math:`h_{L_{floc}}` and :math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta`."
" Fixing these two parameters initially allows us to easily find all other "
"parameters which determine flocculator performance. Here are the current "
"standards (effective 2023) in AguaClara flocculators:"
msgstr ""
"Comenzamos asegurándonos de que nuestro floculador pueda flocular "
"eficazmente definiendo :math:`h_{L_{floc}}` y :math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta`. "
"Fijar estos dos parámetros inicialmente nos permite encontrar fácilmente "
"todos los demás parámetros que determinan el rendimiento del floculador. "
"Aquí están los estándares actuales (efectivos desde 2023) en floculadores "
"AguaClara:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:84
msgid ":math:`\\tilde{G} = 50 Hz`"
msgstr ":math:`\\tilde{G} = 50 Hz`"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:85
msgid ":math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta = 35,000`"
msgstr ":math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta = 35,000`"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:87
msgid ""
"The plant flow rate :math:`Q` is defined by the needs of the community that "
"the plant is being desiged for. Additionally, the height of water *at the "
"end* of the flocculator, :math:`H`, the *maximum* length of the flocculator "
"based on the length of the clarifier length, :math:`L_{max, \\, sed}`, and "
"the *minimum* width of a flocculator channel required for a human to fit "
"inside, :math:`W_{min, \\, human}`, are also defined initially. Ordinarilly "
"in AguaClara plants, the flocculator occupies the same length dimension as "
"the clarifiers, which is why the length constraint exists. See "
":numref:`figure_physical_design_criteria_floc` for a representation of how "
"the flocculator and clarifiers are placed in a plant."
msgstr ""
"El caudal :math:`Q` vegetal se define por las necesidades de la comunidad "
"para la que se diseña la planta. Además, la altura del agua *al final* del "
"floculador, :math:`H`, la *longitud máxima* del floculador basada en la "
"longitud del clarificador, :math:`L_{max, \\, sed}`, y el *mínimo* ancho de "
"un canal de floculador necesario para que un humano encaje dentro, "
":math:`W_{min, \\, human}`, también se definen inicialmente. Normalmente, en"
" las plantas de AguaClara, el floculador ocupa la misma dimensión de "
"longitud que los clarificadores, por lo que existe la restricción de "
"longitud. Véase :numref:`figure_physical_design_criteria_floc` para una "
"representación de cómo se colocan el floculador y los clarificadores en una "
"planta."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:89
msgid ":math:`H = 2 \\, {\\rm m}`"
msgstr ":math:`H = 2 \\, {\\rm m}`"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:90
msgid ":math:`L_{max, \\, sed} = 6 \\, {\\rm m}`"
msgstr ":math:`L_{max, \\, sed} = 6 \\, {\\rm m}`"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:91
msgid ":math:`W_{min, \\, human} = 45 \\, {\\rm cm}`"
msgstr ":math:`W_{min, \\, human} = 45 \\, {\\rm cm}`"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:100
msgid "physical design criteria"
msgstr "Criterios de diseño físico"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:100
msgid ""
"Layout of flocculator and clarifiers that was adopted starting with the 2nd "
"AguaClara plant in Tamara, Honduras in 2008."
msgstr ""
"Diseño del floculador y clarificadores que se adoptó comenzando con la "
"planta 2nd AguaClara en Tamara, Honduras, en 2008."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:103
msgid "Physical Dimensions"
msgstr "Dimensiones físicas"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:104
msgid ""
"Deriving the equations required to find the physical dimensions now and the "
"hydraulic parameters (baffle/obstacle design) in the next section requires "
"many steps. To simplify this design explanation the equation derivations are"
" developed in :ref:`title_review_fluid_mechanics_derivations`. All complex "
"equations which seemingly came out of nowhere will be derived in the "
"derivation sheet."
msgstr ""
"Derivar las ecuaciones necesarias para encontrar las dimensiones físicas "
"ahora y los parámetros hidráulicos (diseño de deflector/obstáculo) en la "
"siguiente sección requiere muchos pasos. Para simplificar esta explicación "
"del diseño, las derivaciones de ecuaciones se desarrollan en "
":ref:`title_review_fluid_mechanics_derivations`. Todas las ecuaciones "
"complejas que aparentemente surgieron de la nada se derivarán en la hoja de "
"derivación."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:107
msgid "Length"
msgstr "Longitud"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:109
msgid ""
"Flocculator length, :math:`L_{channel}`` must meet two constraints: it must "
"be less than or equal to the length of the clarifiers, as the flocculator is"
" adjacent to the clarifier. This constraint is :math:`L_{max, \\, sed}`. "
"Next, the flocculator must be short enough to make sure the target volume of"
" the flocculator is met, while still allowing for a human to fit inside "
":math:`L_{max, \\, \\forall}`. **The constraint that wins out is the one "
"that results in the *smaller* length value**."
msgstr ""
"Longitud floculadora, :math:`L_{channel}`` must meet two constraints: it "
"must be less than or equal to the length of the clarifiers, as the "
"flocculator is adjacent to the clarifier. This constraint is :math:`L_{max, "
"\\, sed}`. Next, the flocculator must be short enough to make sure the "
"target volume of the flocculator is met, while still allowing for a human to"
" fit inside :math:`L_{max, \\, \\forall}`. **La restricción que prevalece es"
" la que da lugar al valor de longitud *smaller***."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:111
msgid ""
"L_{max, \\, sed} = 6 \\, {\\rm m}\n"
"L_{max, \\, \\forall} = \\frac{\\forall}{n_{min, \\, channels} W_{min, \\, "
"human} H}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:116 ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:190
msgid "Such that:"
msgstr "Tal que:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:117
msgid ":math:`n_{min, \\, channels} = 2`"
msgstr ":math:`n_{min, \\, channels} = 2`"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:119
msgid ""
"The reason why :math:`W_{min, \\, human}` is used is because it represents "
"the absolute minimum of flocculator channel width. If the width ends up "
"being larger, the length will decrease. :math:`n_{min, \\, channels} = 2`  "
"to make sure that the flow ends up on the correct side of the clarifier, as "
"the image below shows. Note that there can only be an even number of "
"flocculator channels, as explained in the image's caption."
msgstr ""
"La razón por la que se usa :math:`W_{min, \\, human}` es porque representa "
"el mínimo absoluto del ancho del canal del floculador. Si el ancho resulta "
"mayor, la longitud disminuirá. :math:`n_{min, \\, channels} = 2`  asegurarse"
" de que el flujo acabe en el lado correcto del clarificador, como muestra la"
" imagen de abajo. Ten en cuenta que solo puede haber un número par de "
"canales floculadores, como se explica en el pie de foto de la imagen."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:121
msgid "The equation for *actual* flocculator length is therefore:"
msgstr "La ecuación para la longitud *real* del floculador es, por tanto:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:123
msgid "L_{channel} = {\\rm min}(L_{max, \\, sed}, \\, L_{max, \\, \\forall})"
msgstr "L_{channel} = {\\rm min}(L_{max, \\, sed}, \\, L_{max, \\, \\forall})"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:134
msgid "floc channels"
msgstr "Canales FLOC"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:134
msgid ""
"There are an even amount of flocculator channels to keep the AguaClara plant"
" layout consistent for flows greater than 12 L/s. This ensures that the "
"entrance tank, filter box, and filters can be kept in the same places across"
" plants."
msgstr ""
"Hay una cantidad uniforme de canales floculadores para mantener la "
"disposición de la planta AguaClara consistente en caudales superiores a 12 "
"L/s. Esto garantiza que el tanque de entrada, la caja de filtros y los "
"filtros puedan mantenerse en los mismos lugares entre plantas."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:137
msgid "Width and Number of Channels"
msgstr "Anchura y número de canales"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:139
msgid ""
"The width of a single flocculator channel must meet the following "
"conditions: - Maintain :math:`\\tilde{G}` at the value found in the inputs "
"section - Allow for :math:`3 < \\frac{H_e}{S} < 6`. Recall that "
":math:`\\frac{H_e}{S} =  \\Pi_{H_eS}` - Allow for a human to be able to fit "
"into a flocculator channel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:144
msgid ""
"The first two conditions are wrapped up into the following equation, "
":ref:`which is derived in <title_Flocculation_Derivations>`."
msgstr ""
"Las dos primeras condiciones se envuelven en la siguiente ecuación, "
":ref:`which is derived in <title_Flocculation_Derivations>`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:146
msgid ""
"W_{Min_{H_eS}} = \\frac{\\Pi_{H_eS_{min}}Q}{H_e}\\left( \\frac{K}{2 H_e \\nu"
" \\tilde{G}^2} \\right)^\\frac{1}{3}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:151
msgid ""
"Given that the baffle minor loss coefficient is now known to be a function "
"of :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` we substitute :eq:`K_baffle_expanding`."
msgstr ""
"Dado que ahora se sabe que el coeficiente de pérdida menor del defletor es "
"función de :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` sustituimos :eq:`K_baffle_expanding`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:153
msgid ""
"W_{Min_{H_eS}} = \\frac{\\Pi_{H_eS_{min}}Q}{H_e}\\left( \\frac{ "
"\\left(\\frac{\\left(1 - \\Pi_{vc}^{baffle}\\right) ^ 2}{ \\Pi_{vc}^{baffle}"
" \\Pi_{PlaneJet_{exp}} \\Pi_{H_eS_{min}}}\\right) ^ 2}{2 H_e \\nu "
"\\tilde{G}^2} \\right)^\\frac{1}{3}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:158
msgid ""
"Group the parameters so that the dimensions inside the exponents are a "
"simple as possible."
msgstr ""
"Agrupa los parámetros de modo que las dimensiones dentro de los exponentes "
"sean lo más simples posible."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:160
msgid ""
"W_{Min_{H_eS}} = \\frac{Q}{\\left(\\nu \\tilde{G}^2 "
"H_e^4\\right)^\\frac{1}{3}}\\left( \\frac{ \\left(1 - "
"\\Pi_{vc}^{baffle}\\right) ^ 4 \\Pi_{H_eS_{min}}}{2   \\left( "
"\\Pi_{vc}^{baffle} \\Pi_{PlaneJet_{exp}} \\right)^2} \\right)^\\frac{1}{3}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:166
msgid ""
"This equation represents the absolute smallest width of a flocculator "
"channel if we consider the lowest value of :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` and the "
"highest possible value of :math:`H_e`:"
msgstr ""
"Esta ecuación representa el ancho absoluto menor de un canal floculador si "
"consideramos el valor más bajo de :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` y el valor más alto "
"posible de :math:`H_e`:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:168
msgid ""
":math:`H_e = H_{e_{max}} = H = 2 \\, {\\rm m}`, this implies that there are "
"no obstacles between baffles :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS} = \\Pi_{ {HS}_{min} } = 3`"
msgstr ""
":math:`H_e = H_{e_{max}} = H = 2 \\, {\\rm m}`, esto implica que no hay "
"obstáculos entre los deflectores :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS} = \\Pi_{ {HS}_{min} } = "
"3`"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:171
msgid ""
"Recall our other width constraint, :math:`W_{min, \\, human} = 45 \\, {\\rm "
"cm}`, which is based on our desire to have a human be able to fit into the "
"channels. The governing constraint is the *larger* value of :math:`W_{min}`:"
msgstr ""
"Recuerda nuestra otra restricción de ancho, :math:`W_{min, \\, human} = 45 "
"\\, {\\rm cm}`, que se basa en nuestro deseo de que un humano pueda encajar "
"en los canales. La restricción que rige es el valor *mayor* de "
":math:`W_{min}`:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:173
msgid "W_{min} = {\\rm max}(W_{min, \\, \\Pi_{H_eS}}, \\, W_{min, \\, human})"
msgstr "W_{min} = {\\rm max}(W_{min, \\, \\Pi_{H_eS}}, \\, W_{min, \\, humano})"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:177
msgid ""
"We can find the number of channels, :math:`n_{channels}` and their actual "
"width in one last step, by finding the *total flocculator width* if there "
"were no channels and dividing that by the minimum flocculator width, "
":math:`W_{min}`, found above. The equation for total flocculator width is "
"based on our target volume:"
msgstr ""
"Podemos encontrar el número de canales, :math:`n_{channels}` y su anchura "
"real en un último paso, encontrando el *ancho total del floculador* si no "
"hubiera canales y dividiéndolo por el ancho mínimo del floculador, "
":math:`W_{min}`, hallado arriba. La ecuación para el ancho total del "
"floculador se basa en nuestro volumen objetivo:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:179
msgid "W_{total} = \\frac{\\forall}{H L_{channel}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:183
msgid "Finally:"
msgstr "Por último:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:185
msgid "n_{channels} = \\frac{W_{total}}{W_{min}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:191
msgid ""
":math:`n_{channels}` is an even number and is not 0. Usually, "
":math:`n_{channels}` is either 2 or 4."
msgstr ""
":math:`n_{channels}` es un número par y no es 0. Normalmente, "
":math:`n_{channels}` es 2 o 4."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:193
msgid ""
"Now that we know :math:`n_{channels}`, we can find the actual width of a "
"channel, :math:`W_{channel}`."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que sabemos :math:`n_{channels}`, podemos encontrar el ancho real de "
"un canal, :math:`W_{channel}`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:195
msgid "W_{channel} = \\frac{W_{total}}{n_{channels}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:200
msgid "Hydraulic Parameters"
msgstr "Parámetros hidráulicos"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:202
msgid ""
"Now that the physical dimensions of the flocculator have been defined, the "
"baffle module needs to be designed. The parameter on which most others are "
"based is the distance between flow expansions, :math:`H_e`. Recall that "
":math:`H_e = H` when there are no obstacles in between baffles."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que se han definido las dimensiones físicas del floculador, es "
"necesario diseñar el módulo de deflector. El parámetro en el que se basan la"
" mayoría de los demás es la distancia entre expansiones de flujo, "
":math:`H_e`. Recuerda que :math:`H_e = H` cuando no hay obstáculos entre los"
" deflectores."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:205
msgid "Height Between Expansions"
msgstr "Altura entre expansiones"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:207
msgid ""
"We have a range of possible :math:`H_e` values based on our window of "
":math:`3 < \\frac{H_e}{S} < 6`. However, we have a limitation and a "
"preference which shape how we design :math:`H_e`. Our limitation is that "
"there can only be an integer number of obstacles. Our preference is to have "
"as few obstacles as possible to make the baffle module as easy to fabricate "
"as possible. Therefore, we want :math:`\\frac{H_e}{S}` to be closer to "
":math:`6` than it is to :math:`3`; we are looking for :math:`H_{e_{max}}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:209
msgid ""
"We calculate :math:`H_{e_{max}}` based on the physical flocculator "
"dimensions. The equation for :math:`H_e` is obtained by rearranging Equation"
" :eq:`floc_channel_W_min_var_K`. Because we have already designed the "
"channel width, we substitute :math:`W_{channel}` for :math:`W_{Min_{H_eS}}`."
" Since we are looking for :math:`H_{e_{max}}`, we also substitute "
":math:`\\Pi_{{H_eS}_{max}}` for :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}`. The result is:"
msgstr ""
"Calculamos :math:`H_{e_{max}}` basándonos en las dimensiones físicas del "
"floculador. La ecuación para :math:`H_e` se obtiene reordenando la Ecuación "
":eq:`floc_channel_W_min_var_K`. Como ya hemos diseñado el ancho del canal, "
"sustituimos :math:`W_{channel}` por :math:`W_{Min_{H_eS}}`. Como buscamos "
":math:`H_{e_{max}}`, también sustituimos :math:`\\Pi_{{H_eS}_{max}}` por "
":math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}`. El resultado es:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:211
msgid ""
"H_{e_{max}}^\\frac{4}{3}= \\frac{Q}{W_{Min_{H_eS}} \\left(\\nu \\tilde{G}^2 "
"\\right)^\\frac{1}{3}}\\left( \\frac{ \\left(1 - \\Pi_{vc}^{baffle}\\right) "
"^ 4 \\Pi_{{H_eS}_{max}}}{2   \\left( \\Pi_{vc}^{baffle} "
"\\Pi_{PlaneJet_{exp}} \\right)^2} \\right)^\\frac{1}{3}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:216
msgid "raise to 3/4"
msgstr "Aumento a 3/4"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:218
msgid ""
"H_{e_{max}}= \\left[ \\left(\\frac{Q^3}{W_{Min_{H_eS}}^3 \\nu "
"\\tilde{G}^2}\\right)\\frac{  \\Pi_{{H_eS}_{max}}}{2   \\left( "
"\\Pi_{vc}^{baffle} \\Pi_{PlaneJet_{exp}} \\right)^2} \\right]^\\frac{1}{4} "
"\\left(1 - \\Pi_{vc}^{baffle}\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:223
msgid ""
"For :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` large enough such that the flow has fully expanded "
"the following equation applies."
msgstr ""
"Para :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` lo suficientemente grande como para que el flujo se"
" haya expandido completamente se aplica la siguiente ecuación."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:225
msgid ""
"H_{e_{max}} = \\left[ \\frac{K}{2 \\nu \\tilde{G}^2} \\left( \\frac{Q "
"\\Pi_{{HS}_{max}}}{W_{channel}} \\right)^3 \\right]^\\frac{1}{4}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:230
msgid ""
"Note that this is the *maximum* distance between flow expansions, and does "
"not account for the limitation that there must be an integer number of "
"obstacles per baffle space. Thus, we need to find the *actual* distance "
"between flow expansions. To do this, we determine and round up the number of"
" expansions per baffle space using the ceiling function:"
msgstr ""
"Nótese que esta es la distancia *máxima* entre expansiones de flujo, y no "
"tiene en cuenta la limitación de que debe haber un número entero de "
"obstáculos por espacio de deflector. Por tanto, necesitamos encontrar la "
"distancia *real* entre expansiones de flujo. Para ello, determinamos y "
"redondeamos el número de expansiones por espacio de defletor usando la "
"función techo:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:232
msgid "n_{expansions} = {\\rm ceil}\\left( \\frac{H}{H_{e_{max}}} \\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:236
msgid ""
"If we had used the floor() function instead, we would find that :math:`H_e` "
"would be larger than our upper bound, :math:`H_{e_{max}}`. From here, we can"
" easily get to the actual number of flow expansions per baffle spacing:"
msgstr ""
"Si hubiéramos usado la función floor() en su lugar, encontraríamos que "
":math:`H_e` sería mayor que nuestra cota superior, :math:`H_{e_{max}}`. A "
"partir de aquí, podemos obtener fácilmente el número real de expansiones de "
"flujo por espaciado de los deflectores:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:238
msgid "H_e = \\frac{H}{n_{expansions}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:243
msgid ""
"Finally, we can obtain the number of obstacles per baffle space. The "
":math:`- 1` in the equation is because the baffles themselves provide one "
"flow expansion per baffle space."
msgstr ""
"Finalmente, podemos obtener el número de obstáculos por espacio de "
"deflectores. La :math:`- 1` en la ecuación es que los propios deflectores "
"proporcionan una expansión de flujo por espacio de deflectores."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:245
msgid "n_{obstacles} = \\frac{H}{H_e} - 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:250
msgid "Baffle Spacing"
msgstr "Espaciado de los deflectores"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:252
msgid "Finally, we can find the space between baffles, :math:`S`."
msgstr "Finalmente, podemos encontrar el espacio entre los deflectores, :math:`S`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:256
msgid "Checking the Flocculator Design"
msgstr "Comprobando el diseño del floculador"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:258
msgid ""
"We then compare :math:`n_{spaces, \\, required}` to :math:`n_{spaces, \\, "
"actual}` to make sure that they are equal."
msgstr ""
"Luego comparamos :math:`n_{spaces, \\, required}` con :math:`n_{spaces, \\, "
"actual}` para asegurarnos de que son iguales."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:261
msgid "Average Velocity"
msgstr "Velocidad media"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:263
msgid ""
"As water flows through the flocculators, the flocs will get larger and "
"larger. As a result, their terminal velocity will increase. This is what we "
"want. However, we need to make sure that the flocs don’t settle in the "
"flocculator; that they instead all settle in the clarifier. To make sure of "
"this, we need to make sure that the velocity of water in the flocculator is "
"high enough to scour any flocs that fall to the bottom of the flocculator. "
"The velocity required to scour flocs from the bottom and avoid floc "
"accumulation is around :math:`v_{scour} = 15 \\, {\\rm \\frac{cm}{s}}`. We "
"can check our average velocity :math:`\\bar v` against this value. "
"Unfortunately, the only method to increase the velocity through the "
"flocculator is to increase the space between baffles, S, and decrease the "
"channel width, W. Generally those changes aren't practical and thus there "
"isn't any way to increase the velocity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:265
msgid ""
"\\bar v = \\frac{Q}{W_{channel} S}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:269
msgid "Head loss"
msgstr "Pérdida de carga"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:271
msgid ""
"Head loss is calculated for each expansion using the minor loss coefficient "
"associated with that expansion in Equation :eq:`minor_loss`. The total head "
"loss is simple a sum of the head loss for all of the expansions."
msgstr ""
"pérdida de carga se calcula para cada expansión usando el coeficiente de "
"pérdida menor asociado a esa expansión en la ecuación :eq:`minor_loss`. El "
"pérdida de carga total es simplemente, la suma de los pérdida de carga para "
"todas las expansiones."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:274
msgid "Residence Time"
msgstr "Tiempo de residencia"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:276
msgid ""
"It is now time to make our final check. We need to make sure that our actual"
" residence time is *at least* as much as we designed for. Fortunately, in "
"our design we did not account for the change in water level throughout the "
"flocculator due to head loss. Therefore, the actual volume of water in the "
"flocculator is actually greater than :math:`\\forall_{floc}`. See "
":numref:`figure_flocculator_head_loss` for clarification."
msgstr ""
"Ahora es momento de hacer la comprobación final. Debemos asegurarnos de que "
"el tiempo real de residencia sea *al menos* el que hemos previsto. "
"Afortunadamente, en nuestro diseño no tuvimos en cuenta el cambio de nivel "
"del agua en todo el floculador debido a pérdida de carga. Por lo tanto, el "
"volumen real de agua en el floculador es en realidad mayor que "
":math:`\\forall_{floc}`. Consulta :numref:`figure_flocculator_head_loss` "
"para aclarar."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:285
msgid "Flocculator_head_loss"
msgstr "Flocculator_head_loss"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:285
msgid ""
"The water level in the flocculator decreases due to head loss. Flocculators "
"may occupy multiple channels, but this extra triangle of water exists in any"
" case."
msgstr ""
"La nivel del agua en el floculador disminuye debido a pérdida de carga. Los "
"floculadores pueden ocupar múltiples canales, pero este triángulo extra de "
"agua existe en cualquier caso."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:288
msgid ""
"Thus, the actual average water level in the flocculator is :math:`H + "
"\\frac{h_{L_{floc}}}{2}`. Thus, the actual residence time is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:290
msgid ""
"\\theta_{actual} = \\frac{n_{channels} L_{channel} W_{channel} \\left( H + "
"\\frac{h_{L_{floc}}}{2} \\right)} {Q}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Design.rst:292
msgid "Check to see if :math:`\\theta_{actual}` is greater than :math:`\\theta`."
msgstr "Comprueba si :math:`\\theta_{actual}` es mayor que :math:`\\theta`."

